<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kuru Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1200 BCE – 350 BCE (approx.) · capital Hastinapura</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The leading kingdom of the Middle Vedic period, where the Vedic hymns were collected and the ritual order of early Hinduism took shape.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kuru tribe formed in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-yamuna-doab">Ganges-Yamuna Doab</a> around 1200 BCE, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bharatas">Bharata</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purus">Puru</a> clans merged into a single polity. Under kings remembered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atharvaveda">Atharvaveda</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmanas">Brahmanas</a>, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parikshit">Parikshit</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janamejaya">Janamejaya</a>, it became the dominant power of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, with centres at Asandivat and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hastinapura">Hastinapura</a>. Many historians regard it as the first state-level society in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kuru kings patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> priests, who arranged the hymns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a> into collections and developed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaveda">Samaveda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yajurveda">Yajurveda</a>. Royal consecration rites such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasuya">Rajasuya</a> and the horse sacrifice reinforced kingship, and society was ordered into the four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">varnas</a>. The economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herding, barley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farming, and the early use of iron. Memories of the kingdom later formed the backdrop of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tradition says a flood of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> drove the court from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hastinapura">Hastinapura</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kausambi">Kaushambi</a>. By the 6th century BCE the Kurus were a minor mahajanapada, partly ruled as a sangha, overshadowed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kosala">Kosala</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a>. Their territory was absorbed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nanda-empire">Nanda Empire</a> in the 4th century BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kuru-kingdom.jpg" alt="Kuru Kingdom" width="320" height="269"><figcaption>Image: Roshan Krishna Dhanawade (Srimant ROSHAN) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Kuru_Kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1200 BCE – 350 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hastinapura</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Parikshit, Janamejaya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vedic Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuru, Kuru Mahajanapada</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-775&amp;focus=kuru-kingdom" aria-label="Kuru Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6714 1107 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kuru Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7034 1363L7253 1492"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7253 1492h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7034 1363h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7034 136